 ## Background
-NeRFifyMesh was introduced to address the need for tools to convert existing 3D mesh models into NeRF representations for rapid algorithm development and testing, particularly in robotics [S1, unofficial]. It builds on the principles of [Radiance-field optimization](44-radiance-field-optimization.md) but diverges by using mesh-derived ground truth instead of image-based optimization. The method leverages hash encoding inspired by [Instant-NGP](1414-hierarchical-grid-optimization.md) and SIREN networks for color/normal prediction [S1, unofficial].
